# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# APERTURE — environment variables
# Copy to `.env.local` for local dev, or configure in Vercel Project Settings.
# Every value below with a ⇨ arrow is a plug-and-play slot — fill in before deploy.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# n8n webhook that the Vercel /api/donate route forwards to.
# ⇨ Create a Webhook trigger in n8n (see n8n/aperture-workflow.json), copy its
#   Production URL here. Leave trailing slash OFF.
#   Example: https://<n8n-host>/webhook/aperture-donate
N8N_WEBHOOK_URL=

# Shared secret sent in X-Aperture-Token header so random callers can't
# invoke the workflow. Set the SAME value in the n8n workflow's "Verify Token"
# IF node. Any long random string is fine.
# ⇨ Generate with: `openssl rand -hex 32`
APERTURE_SHARED_TOKEN=

# Optional: show this location tag in the UI and include in n8n payloads.
NEXT_PUBLIC_LOCATION_LABEL=Cul2vate — Ellington Ag Center

# Where the bias-table JSON is served. n8n fetches this at each run to apply
# per-class weight correction multipliers. Defaults to the Vercel /bias-table.json
# after your first deploy — the training-loop rewrites the file, you redeploy.
# ⇨ Paste your Vercel production URL here after `vercel --prod`:
#   Example: https://<vercel-app-host>/bias-table.json
BIAS_TABLE_URL=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The following live inside the n8n workflow, NOT in this .env — but listed
# here so you know exactly which credentials to have ready when you open n8n:
#
#   HIKVISION_CAMERA_URL        Public snapshot endpoint.
#                                ⇨ Point this at the Aperture Bridge service
#                                   running on your Dell G7:
#                                   https://aperture-bridge.<your-domain>/snapshot
#                                   (see bridge/setup-dell.sh + docs/BRIDGE-DEPLOY.md)
#   BRIDGE_TOKEN                Bearer token the bridge validates on /snapshot.
#                                Must match /etc/aperture-bridge.env on the Dell.
#   VISION_MODEL_PROVIDER       openai | anthropic | google
#   OPENAI_API_KEY              (if using OpenAI)
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY           (if using Claude)
#   FARMBRITE_API_BASE               https://api.farmbrite.com/v1
#   FARMBRITE_API_KEY                Farmbrite → Settings → Developers → New API Key
#   FARMBRITE_INVENTORY_TYPE_ID      ID of the "Aperture Donations" inventory_type
#                                     (auto-created by discover-farmbrite-endpoint.sh)
#   FARMBRITE_LOCATION_ID            ID of the Farmbrite location to credit the
#                                     donation to (Ellington Ag Center, etc.)
#   APERTURE_LOG_SHEET_ID            Google Sheet ID for the running donation log
#                                     (create a sheet named "Donations" with headers
#                                      triggered_at, location, description, item_type,
#                                      inside_zone, charuco_detected, weight_lbs,
#                                      weight_lbs_raw, weight_lbs_low, weight_lbs_high,
#                                      bias_multiplier, confidence, known_failure_flags,
#                                      notes, prompt_version, model)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
